Cody eats three times as many cookies as Amir eats. This means Cody eats 3 * the number of cookies Amir eats. Since Amir eats 5 cookies, Cody eats 3 * 5 = 15 cookies.

To find out how many cookies they eat together, we add the number of cookies Cody eats and the number of cookies Amir eats. So, they eat 15 + 5 = 20 cookies together.

\boxed{20}

